<section class="hql-band hql-band--playground" markdown>

# Playground { .hql-play-title }

HQL runs in this page. A program is checked and evaluated in your browser;
nothing is sent to a server. The vault is the book's
[[21-a-vault|reading club]]: `cards`, `@[[dune]]` and the links between them
are there to query.

<div class="hql-playground" data-hql-playground hidden>
<div class="hql-play-bar">
<label>Program <select aria-label="Example program"></select></label>
<span class="hql-play-buttons">
<button type="button" class="hql-run" data-how="check">Check</button>
<button type="button" class="hql-run hql-run--primary" data-how="eval">Run</button>
</span>
</div>
<textarea spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="off" autocomplete="off" aria-label="HQL program" rows="18"></textarea>
<pre class="hql-output" aria-live="polite">Press Run, or Ctrl+Enter.</pre>

</div>

<div class="hql-examples" markdown>

```hql title="A typed query"
type Book { title : String, year : Int, rating : Int }

books = [
    Book(title = "Dune", year = 1965, rating = 5),
    Book(title = "Emma", year = 1815, rating = 3),
    Book(title = "Beloved", year = 1987, rating = 4),
]

books
| filter(b => b.rating >= 4)
| sort(b => b.title)
| map(b => b.title)
```

```hql title="A contract refuses a value"
type Book { title : String, year : Int, rating : Int }

books = [
    Book(title = "Dune", year = 1965, rating = 5),
    Book(title = "Emma", year = "1815", rating = 3),
]

books | map(b => b.title)
```

```hql title="The vault: books still to read"
cards
| filter(c => c.metadata.status == "todo")
| sort(by = c => c.title)
| map(c => c.title)
```

```hql title="The vault: one card"
@[[dune]].title
```

```hql title="The vault: authors as Markdown"
cards | filter(c => c.metadata.category == "author") | markdown
```

</div>

<noscript markdown>
The playground needs JavaScript. Without it, these are its programs; each is
in the [[book|HQL Book]] with its output.
</noscript>

## What runs here { .hql-section }

The language, the standard library and SQLite, in memory. A program that
names a server (a `postgres`, `kafka`, `nats` or `spark` endpoint, or a
URL) checks, and fails where it would connect: those run in the
[hql-demo repository](https://github.com/ewiger/hql-demo). Files on your
machine are not read.

</section>
